@startuml
title GhostHouses Stage B Deployment Environment

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam wrapWidth 220
left to right direction

actor "Municipality Users\n(private network)" as users
actor "IT / DB Admin" as admin

cloud "Public registries\n(build time only)" as registries {
  component "Docker Hub\nnode:20\nnginx:alpine" as dockerhub
  component "Microsoft Container Registry\n.NET SDK/ASP.NET 8" as mcr
}

node "Municipality Windows Server VM" as vm {
  frame "Docker Compose\nproject/docker-compose.yml" as compose {
    component "Frontend container\nNginx + React build\nHost port: 443 HTTPS\nContainer port: 443 HTTPS\nNetwork: app-net" as frontend

    component "Backend container\nASP.NET Core API\nHost port: none\nContainer port: 8080 HTTP\nNetworks: app-net + db-net" as backend

    database "PostgreSQL container\nDatabase\nHost port: none\nContainer port: 5432 TCP\nNetworks: db-net + admin-net\nVolume: db-data" as postgres

    component "pgAdmin container\nDatabase admin UI\nHost port: 8443 HTTPS\nContainer port: 443 HTTPS\nNetwork: admin-net\nVolume: pgadmin-data" as pgadmin
  }
}

users --> frontend : HTTPS 443
admin --> pgadmin : HTTPS 8443

frontend --> backend : HTTP 8080\n/api requests
backend --> postgres : PostgreSQL 5432\nEF Core / Npgsql
pgadmin --> postgres : PostgreSQL 5432\nadmin access

registries ..> compose : docker compose up -d --build\npull/build dependencies

note right of frontend
Only public application entry point.
Normal users do not access backend or DB directly.
end note

note bottom of backend
Internal-only API.
No host port mapping.
end note

note bottom of postgres
Internal-only database.
No host port mapping.
end note

legend bottom
|= Docker Network |= Members |= Purpose |
| app-net | Frontend, Backend | Web app to API only |
| db-net | Backend, PostgreSQL | API to database only |
| admin-net | pgAdmin, PostgreSQL | Database administration only |

External exposed ports:
Frontend HTTPS 443, pgAdmin HTTPS 8443.
Backend 8080 and PostgreSQL 5432 are internal to Docker.
endlegend

@enduml
